ose into a counter and  can count the number of any particular  the number of barcodes that they have  for each of the genes that are  expressing in your section  so that's the sort of basic concept of  the um of the nano strings and i think  it becomes the mana string technology  and i think it becomes uh even clearer  when you see what our experiment is  so the idea of the experiment  is to assess the effect of the vicinity  to the plaque on gene expression so as i  said we've shown already that microglia  of genes are expressed or that a bunch  of microbial genes expressed in  incredibly close correlation with the  buildup of plaques so we want to know  whether it's just that they're only  expressed when they're near the plaque  or whether they're expressed generally  in the tissue and exactly how those  how those genes interact with the plaque  we've mostly worked on microglia but now  we're starting to work a lot on  astrocytes as well the other sort of  another sort of immune cell in the brain  and so what we've done here is looked  specifically at the gene expression in  microglia or the gene expression in  astrocytes and we've looked compared to  where they are sitting in relation to  plaques now i should say at this point  that it's important to make clear that  you're not actually doing single cell  rna-seq effectively you're not actually  collecting  just from microglia it's going to be  highly enriched for microglia but what  it's doing is you label the microglial  cell and then it cleaves  in that place where that label is so if  anything is just below or just above it  will collect that rna also extremely  enriched for the cells because the  sections are only eight microns thick  and that's pretty much the thickness of  a single cell so they're very highly  enriched for microglia or very highly in  which for alzheimer's sorry for  astrocytes excuse me um in our in our  study  so we're looking at different mouse  models we have wild-type mice the  ordin