h to  see what happens in terms of the plaques  but also to see how the trim to 47h  mutation  affects this  this is a this was just a trial study  using the tap program at um at  nanostring so this is just a very first  trial we're going to repeat this and  increase the numbers  so what we had in the first instance was  three wild-type mice three trim two mice  so they're the mice that don't have  plaques and then we had four each of the  plaque bearing mice the nlf and the nlf  trim two  so these uh unfortunately in the in the  process we lost the the information from  two of the mice so we ended up with two  three three four three as our sample  size a total of 14 mice a total of 12  giving us information  this is quite a small sample size we're  very keen to increase this but it is  remarkable how much information we've  already got even from this small sample  size  now how the system works is that you  have a slide like this this is a  standard sized slide  and you see that there's an area there  marked out 36.2 by 14.6 millimeters  and your sections have to fit within  that area  how the analysis is costed when you're  working with the tap program and it  varies depending on how you're doing  this but when you're working with the  nanostringstat program how this  works is that you  pay per slide  and each slide comes with 12 regions of  interest or areas of interest  and you can then pay for extra areas of  interest in lots of 12.  so  you can however fit as many sections as  you like on a slide or as you can  reasonably fit within that area of 36.2  by 14.6 millimeters  we managed to fit the 14 sections so one  section from each of those 14 mice onto  two slides so we had one slide with  eight that did  the schematic on the top of that and one  slide with six  sections and as you can see we have a  mixture of the genotypes on each of the  slides to try and avoid any batch  effects and so forth  on those slides we there the slides then  look like this basical